Lucciola: keep the login form still when a message arrives

The panel is centred on the screen and its height followed its contents, so
the fingerprint prompt arriving on the status line grew the panel and pushed
the whole form up by half a line (24 physical pixels at 2880x1920, measured on
screenshots before and after the message). The user's name above the field and
the choice between the password and the user picker moved it in the same way.

Every part now keeps its room whether or not it has something to show: the
status line, the name, and the taller of the two forms. The status line stays
one line, with an ellipsis for what does not fit: wrapping would move the form
again. The messages seen in practice fit (the panel takes about 60 characters).

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.6.0 tag, after
0005. Could be proposed upstream (noctalia-dev/noctalia-greeter).

